      "claim": "SCH39304, a close triazole antifungal analogue sharing the tertiary alcohol, triazole, and difluorophenyl core with the query, showed 57% serum-to-CSF penetration in animals after a 20 mg/kg dose, with drug measurable in CSF even in the absence of meningeal inflammation. This directly supports meaningful CNS access for the query under meningitis.",
